{
  "Brief notifications at the edge of the window, with four tones, an optional action such as Undo, a custom duration or none, six positions and a limit on how many appear at once. Show them programmatically, or place a custom region in JSX.": "",
  "Programmatic and declarative use": "",
  "`toast.show()` and its tone shortcuts return a `Toast` object that you can `close()`, `update()` or await. They use `Toaster.default`, which is created in `document.body` on first use. An application can place its own `Toaster` anywhere in JSX and make it the default.": "",
  "`tone` sets the glyph, its color, and how screen readers announce the toast: politely for `info` and `success`, and immediately for `caution` and `danger`.": "",
  "Action and Undo": "Action ve Geri al",
  "`action` adds a button that runs `click` and then closes the toast. Offering Undo is usually better than asking for confirmation first.": "",
  "Duration and updates": "",
  "`duration` is 5 seconds by default, and `0` keeps the toast open until it is closed. Every option also accepts a function, and `update()` changes a visible toast and restarts its timer.": "",
  "Positions": "Konumlar",
  "There are six positions, and start and end follow the reading direction. The newest toast is closest to the edge. A toast's `position` takes precedence over the toaster's.": "",
  "Custom toaster and max": "",
  "A `Toaster` is the region toasts appear in. `max` limits how many appear at once in one position, and the rest wait until others close. This one is placed directly in the page, so Tab reaches its toasts after these buttons.": "",
  "From anywhere on the page, moves focus to the newest toast. Inside a toast, returns focus to where it was.": "",
  "Moves through the toasts and their buttons. The default toaster is the last element on the page, so Tab reaches it after the page content.": "",
  "With focus in a toast, closes it. Focus moves to the next toast, or back to where it came from.": "",
  "`<section role=\"region\">` named \"Notifications\" (`uiLocale`), with `aria-keyshortcuts` for the hotkey.": "Kısayol için `aria-keyshortcuts` taşıyan, \"Bildirimler\" (`uiLocale`) adlı `<section role=\"region\">`.",
  "Info and success toasts are announced politely (`role=\"status\"`), and caution and danger toasts immediately (`role=\"alert\"`). `update()` announces the toast again. A live `text` function does not, so a progress number is not read on every change.": "",
  "A toast never takes focus. Each one is a group named by its title and text, and has its own Tab stop, so toasts without buttons can also be reached.": "",
  "Timers stop while the pointer or focus is on the toasts and while the page is hidden (WCAG 2.2.1). Use `duration: 0` for anything the user must act on.": "İşaretçi ya da odak toast'lardayken ve sayfa gizliyken zamanlayıcılar durur (WCAG 2.2.1). Kullanıcının karşılık vermesi gereken her şey için `duration: 0` kullanın.",
  "It slides in and fades out using the motion tokens. When the user prefers reduced motion, it appears without animation.": "",
  "The names of the region and the close button come from `uiLocale.strings` (`notifications`, `close`) and update immediately.": "",
  "The region.": "Bölge.",
  "A stack at one position. `data-position`.": "Bir konumdaki yığın. `data-position`.",
  "A toast. `data-tone`, `data-state` (`entering`, `shown`, `leaving`).": "Toast. `data-tone`, `data-state` (`entering`, `shown`, `leaving`).",
  "Its buttons (Button, `sm`).": "",
  "The width of a toast, which never exceeds the window.": "",
  "The distance to the window edge, and how far the toast slides in from it (at a corner, also from the side).": "",
  "The alignment of the action and close buttons.": "",
  "Units: the space between toasts, and the toast with its box per tone (`success`, `caution`, `danger`) and for keyboard focus (`focus`).": "",
  "Optional units: a stripe along the start edge, and a line that shrinks with the remaining time, per tone.": "",
  "Units: the tone glyph and a plate behind it, per tone, and the tone's own mark.": "",
  "Units: the title, the message and the spacing around the buttons. Their appearance comes from the `action` and `close` places.": "",
  "Toast options and props": "Toast seçenekleri ve prop'ları",
  "The message.": "İleti.",
  "A bold line above the message.": "",
  "`info`, `success`, `caution` or `danger`, which set the glyph, its color and how screen readers announce the toast.": "",
  "The tone glyph": "",
  "A custom icon, or `null` for none.": "",
  "The time it stays, in milliseconds. `0` keeps it open until it is closed.": "",
  "`{ text, click }` adds a button to the toast, such as Undo. It runs `click(toast)` and then closes the toast.": "",
  "Shows a close button named from `uiLocale`.": "",
  "From the toaster": "",
  "The stacking position: `top-start`, `top`, `top-end`, `bottom-start`, `bottom` or `bottom-end`.": "",
  "See Events.": "",
  "toast and Toast": "toast ve Toast",
  "Shows a toast on `Toaster.default`.": "`Toaster.default` üzerinde toast gösterir.",
  "Same as `show`, with the tone already set.": "",
  "Closes every toast on `Toaster.default`.": "",
  "Closes the toast. A closed toast is disposed.": "",
  "Changes any options, restarts the timer and announces the toast again.": "",
  "Resolves when the toast closes, with `timeout`, `button`, `escape`, `action` or `code`.": "",
  "The same information as an event.": "",
  "Every option is also a property that accepts a value or a function.": "",
  "Toaster props": "Toaster prop'ları",
  "The stacking position, unless a toast specifies its own.": "",
  "The number of toasts shown at once in one position. The rest wait their turn.": "",
  "Moves focus to the newest toast and back again. Use `''` for none.": "",
  "Pauses timers while the pointer is over the toasts. Timers always stop while focus is inside them or the page is hidden.": "",
  "`uiLocale` strings": "",
  "The name of the region.": "Bölgenin adı.",
  "Toaster members": "Toaster üyeleri",
  "The toaster used by `toast`, created in `document.body` on first use, or the one you assign.": "",
  "Same as on `toast`, for this toaster.": "",
  "Moves focus to the newest toast.": "Odağı en yeni toast'a taşır.",
  "The toasts on screen, followed by the waiting ones.": "",
